    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to bolster our stolen base totals. **Kyle Tucker** (72.53) leads the charge as our strongest play, benefiting significantly from a generous SP_xERA of 4.54 against Peralta and providing a high-floor offensive engine. He is flanked by **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Heliot Ramos** (70.57), both of whom receive massive boosts from park factors and weak opposing starters (Ray and Sullivan, respectively). **Andy Pages** (69.99) is another high-conviction start, as the combination of his second-hole placement and favorable delivery metrics against Peralta positions him to capitalize on early-inning scoring opportunities. **Gunnar Henderson** (64.31) remains a mandatory start despite facing a tougher arm in Greene, as his dynamic platoon advantage and leadoff role provide enough efficiency to justify the inclusion.\n\nStrategic adjustments were required to maintain our SB-focused efficiency, which led to the difficult decision to bench **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.46). While his talent is undeniable, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold when compared to the platoon-advantaged **Josh Lowe** (59.89) and **Liam Hicks** (59.93). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** was ultimately benched due to a restrictive park factor and a poor matchup against Gilbert, which compressed his projected ceiling compared to the primary lineup. We are monitoring the status of **Jackson Merrill** (51.61) closely; his matchup against Yamamoto is statistically difficult, and his reduced score reflects an \"Elite Hold\" warning\u2014the opposing pitcher's high efficiency in controlling the run game makes him a liability for our SB-first strategy. Owners should proceed with caution regarding the wind and potential lineup shifts, as any deviation in batting order for **Liam Hicks** or **Heliot Ramos** could necessitate a recalibration of these daily efficiency scores.",
